mission "The Drowned Crown Coordinates"
    name "The Drowned Crown Coordinates"
    description "Use the register and tideglass to calculate the position of the drowned settlement."
    source "Nueva Esperanza"
    destination "Bellweather Cay"
    reward 1525
    speaker offer "Doctor Inez Salvatierra"
    speaker visit "Doctor Inez Salvatierra"
    speaker complete "Doctor Inez Salvatierra"
    to offer
        has "The King's Unwritten Order: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `Doctor Inez has set the tideglass beside the old register. Its markings shift as the water level changes, and a set of coordinates is beginning to emerge.`
            `Inez checks the register against the tideglass. "The register gives us the old measurements; the tideglass gives us the correction. With both, we can calculate where the drowned settlement lies."`
            choice
                `"I will lend a hand. Tell me where to begin."`
                    accept
                `"There is more here than you have told me. What is it?"`
                    goto details
                `"I will not put my crew between old enemies."`
                    close
            label details
                `She marks the hour beside the figures. "The margin notes are precise, but only if the tide is read at the right time. Sail to the marked water and take the readings before the current turns."`
                choice
                    `"Then you have my word. I will see it through."`
                        accept
                    `"Then we part here. Fair winds."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Drowned Crown Coordinates. Use the register and tideglass to calculate the position of the drowned settlement."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Bellweather Cay, Inez works through the figures against the register. The corrected readings place the drowned settlement beyond the western shoals. "There," she says, tapping the chart. "Not a legend after all. A place, with a position."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Inez puts the finished calculations away. "We have coordinates, not permission to claim the place. The people who live around those waters must have a say before anyone calls it a discovery."`
        log "Completed The Drowned Crown Coordinates. Received 1525 gold. Use the register and tideglass to calculate the position of the drowned settlement."
